## 0. HEADLINE

The QGenodeScreen 1x1-stale race (Phase 11 suspected race; "panel
degenerate ~1x28 / black" symptom) **DID NOT REPRODUCE** in any of
the 10 cold-boot trials on the current tree (W3's focused reproducer,
base-sel4 on QEMU/KVM). All 10 trials are `clean`. Per D14.8(b):
candidate (b) is **Re-scoped to Phase 15+**. No vendored-tree patch
lands in Phase 14 (W3 is investigation only — AGENTS.md §5.2).

  Race-reproduction count: 0 / 10  (D14.8(b) threshold: >= 3 / 10)
  Classification outcome:  Re-scoped to Phase 15+
  Vendored-tree patches applied in W3: NONE  (AGENTS.md §5.2 / plan)

The Phase 11 fix (panel_widget.cc::_apply_geometry width-floor;
`screen_w > 64 ? screen_w : 1024`) holds on this topology: every
trial shows `race_panel_black_max=0` (the panel band was never black,
so the QPA's 1x1 transient never reached sponge-de's panel widget in
a way that pinned it to a degenerate buffer).

================================================================================
1. WHAT W3 ADDED
================================================================================

  - repos/sponge/src/test/qscreen_race_probe/target.mk        (NEW)
  - repos/sponge/src/test/qscreen_race_probe/main.cc           (NEW)
    — a small plain-Genode component (no libc, no Qt). Opens a
      Capture session, allocates the 1024x768 capture buffer as
      early as possible (defines nitpicker's panorama, mirroring
      fb_sdl's role in the interactive scenario). Reads the FIRST
      capture sample at (512, 14) [panel band] and (512, 412) [demo
      domain center], then polls a bounded 60s cold-boot window
      (300 iters x 200 ms) for the demo-domain themed window_bg
      (#313244, from default.theme) to appear. Verdict:
        - "trial verdict clean" if window_bg observed within the
          budget (race did NOT reproduce this boot).
        - "trial verdict race"  if window_bg never observed within
          the budget AND the panel band reads 0x0 (the 1x28-degenerate
          race signature).
      The probe always exits 0 (the run script gates on the regex,
      not on the exit code — D14.8(b)'s >= 3/10 reproduction
      threshold is a counting policy in the evidence log, not a
      hard pass/fail gate).

  - run/sponge-de-qscreen-race-probe.run                     (NEW)
    — focused reproducer. Topology mirrors the proven reference
      run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run (drivers sub-init +
      sponge-de) but MINUS the launch/inject plumbing (no
      sponge_pkgd, no pkg_runtime, no input-relay ROM, no QMP
      choreography). The only variable under test is cold-boot
      timing; QMP machinery would introduce its own timing noise.
    — build list includes `core lib/ld init timer server/report_rom
      server/nitpicker driver/acpi app/pci_decode driver/platform
      driver/framebuffer/vesa driver/ps2 driver/usb_host/pc
      driver/usb_hid server/event_filter sponge-de
      test/qscreen_race_probe qt6/base ...` — the proven reference
      caps sizing (sponge-de `caps: 1000 | ram: 128M`,
      qscreen_race_probe `caps: 100 | ram: 16M`).
    — gates:
        run_genode_until {.*\[init -> drivers -> fb\] using 1024x768.*} 90
        run_genode_until {.*qscreen-race-probe: trial verdict (clean|race).*} 90

  - repos/sponge/run/sponge-de-qscreen-race-probe.run
    — committed relative symlink -> ../../../run/sponge-de-qscreen-race-probe.run
    (matches the same symlink pattern used by every other run script
    in this repo so the Genode repo-discovery picks it up regardless
    of build launch directory).

