7. NOTES ON THE REPRODUCER'S DESIGN
================================================================================

  - Topology match to the proven reference. The scenario's build
    list and init config mirror run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run
    MINUS the launch plumbing. Cold-boot timing is therefore the
    same as the proven reference's first boot — which is where the
    Phase 11 race was suspected (heavy alpha topology).
  - No QMP. The Phase 10 / Phase 12 QMP machinery (TCP listener +
    qmp_connect + expect round-trips) would add its own timing
    noise; the race is purely a cold-boot timing-class symptom and
    must be measured against an idle boot. QMP-driven clicks can be
    added in a future Phase 15+ probe if a "QMP-click-during-cold-
    boot" variant is needed.
  - No pkg_runtime / sponge_pkgd. Sponge-de's launcher backend
    defaults to "none" (logs "launcher source=none; panel button
    will report 'not attached'") which is the same code path that
    was exercised pre-W3 (no packages pre-installed).
  - No input drivers bound. The run scenario drops usb_hid binding
    (no `-device nec-usb-xhci` / `-device usb-tablet` QEMU args),
    so usb_hid has nothing to bind and stays quiet. This is the
    deliberate scoping decision documented in the run script's
    gate-comment block.
  - The 60s bounded window (300 polls x 200 ms) is generous on
    purpose — a CLEAN verdict should arrive within 1-3 polls
    (~200-600 ms) on this host. The 60s ceiling is there so a
    future regression (e.g., the width-floor guard is removed or
    weakened) would still record a `race` verdict within the run
    budget rather than timing out the run script.
  - The probe exits 0 on both verdicts intentionally. D14.8(b)'s
    ">= 3 of 10 trials" policy is applied by THIS evidence log,
    not by a hard pass/fail gate on the run script. A non-zero
    exit on `race` would be a louder hard-gate, but it would also
    contradict the plan's "investigation only" framing and force
    the run tool to retry on any race verdict.